<title>USA: Buffalo, N.Y., $83 mln RANs priced by First Albany.</title>
<headline>Buffalo, N.Y., $83 mln RANs priced by First Albany.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Albany Corp said Tuesday it tentatively priced $83 million of Buffalo, N.Y., revenue anticipation notes with a 3.60 percent yield.</p>
<p>The notes have a 4.25 percent coupon and are rated MIG-1 by Moody's Investors Service and SP1-plus by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>The notes are dated 11/15/196 and due 7/15/1997.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
